+// manyFilesHelp is a prototype for roamer7038/wikictl-eval: how to read many
+// files without one command per file.
+const manyFilesHelp = `Reading many files:
+  Each command fetches before it reads, which takes a few hundred
+  milliseconds; a loop of one command per file over hundreds of files takes
+  minutes. Instead, pass all paths to one cat, stat or ls -l:
+    wikictl find <dir> -name '*.md' | tr '\n' '\0' |
+      xargs -0 -r wikictl cat --json
+  and pick values with jq from items[] {path, sha, content}. Narrow first with
+  grep -l, grep -c or find -meta KEY=VALUE. For a repository nobody writes to
+  during the task, add --no-fetch after the first command. Print paths or
+  counts first, and read only what you need.
+`
+
